sentences.text:
...RESPONDENTS (BY SMT. RATNA N. SHIVAYOGIMATH, ADVOCATE  FOR R1 TO R3;
 R4 AND R5 SERVED  R2 AND R3 ARE MINOR REPRESENTED BY R1;)
 THIS MFA IS FILED UNDER SECTION 173 (1) OF THE MOTOR VEHICLES ACT, PRAYING TO SET ASIDE THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED 06.10.2018 IN MVC NO.1141/2013 PASSED BY THE II ADDL. DISTRICT AND SESSIONS JUDGE AND MACT-VI, VIJAYAPUR, BY ALLOWING THE ABOVE APPEAL.

Taking into consideration the material on record, I am of the view that, the claim petition has been filed before the Tribunal fraudulently to seek the compensation by implicating the vehicle in question and in the light of the observation made above, I pass the following:
ORDER (i) MFA No.202132/2019 is allowed in part;
(ii) MFA No.200955/2019 is dismissed;
NC: 2026:KHC-K:1110 HC-KAR (iii) The Judgment and award dated 06.10.2018 passed in MVC No.1141/2013 by the Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Vijayapura is hereby set aside and the claim petition filed by the claimants is dismissed;
Smt. Rekha And Ors vs Satish Bhairu Raut And Anr on 5 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/92654612/
